.SS "int cache_load (\fBq_element\fP * q, char * fn)"
.PP
cache_load - load a file containing the cache for a folder do not call \fBmodel_evt()\fP from within; we're called by the scanner rather than the GUI thread! 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIq\fP - the directory the contents of which are to be loaded 
.br
\fIfn\fP - the path and name of the file to load
.RE
.PP

.SS "cache_el* cache_load_el (int fd, ulong * len)"
.PP
cache_load_el - load a single cache-element from a cache-file. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
the address of the new cache-element's header (which must be freed). the data begin directly after the returned header (and will be free()d along with the header). 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIfd\fP - the file-descriptor for the cache-file to save in 
.br
\fIlen\fP - where (if non-NULL) the number of data-bytes read will be stored, excluding the length of the header
.RE
.PP

.SS "static int cache_save (\fBfile_info\fP * dir, char * name)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
cache_save - save a cache-file for a folder 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIdir\fP - the directory to save a cache-file for 
.br
\fIname\fP - the (hashed) name and path of the cache-file
.RE
.PP

.SS "static ulong cache_save_el (int fd, char * tag, ulong len, void * data)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
cache_save_el - save a single entry in cache. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
the number of characters written (length_of_data + length_of_header) 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIfd\fP - the file-descriptor for the cache-file to save in 
.br
\fItag\fP - tag describing the type of the entry 
.br
\fIlen\fP - the size of the entry (excluding its header) 
.br
\fIdata\fP - the data to write (len bytes)
.RE
.PP

